WHAT THIS COVERS

This repository holds two different kinds of thing under one roof, and the difference decides
what you may do. Read the group your file is in.

  1. CODE — everything under src/ and prova/, plus construir.mjs, package.json and the built
     index.html. Licensed under the GNU Affero General Public License, version 3.
     Full text: LICENSE-AGPL-3.0.txt.

  2. SAMPLES — samples/sigils/, samples/sigils-black/, samples/contact-sheet.svg, and the WAV
     files under samples/audio/.

  3. OPEN SET — the 100 SVG files under samples/open-set/. Generated from seeds reserved for
     publication; they belong to no set offered for sale.

  4. GALLERY — the raster images under samples/gallery/. These DEPICT pieces that are not
     published here and are not licensed by this document. They are provided so the engine's
     output can be seen at scale, for viewing only. No right to use, extract, trace, reproduce
     or redistribute the depicted pieces is granted by their appearance in these images, and no
     such right may be inferred from it.

THE CODE — GROUP 1

Free software under the AGPL-3.0. You may run it, read it, change it and redistribute it. If you
modify it and let others use it over a network, the AGPL requires you to offer them your modified
source as well.

A separate commercial licence, for anyone who needs this code inside a closed product, is held by
the authors and available from them. The dual arrangement is deliberate: the tool is open so that
anyone can use it and check it, while the right to build a closed product on it stays with
Nthnkr "dpna" and AmandaBT.

THE GENERATIVE ENGINE IS NOT PUBLISHED HERE, and no code in this repository contains it. The tool
draws no sigils. It selects among the 100 already-published files of the open set, by a
deterministic code derived from the figures being signed. The engine that produced those files
remains unpublished and is licensed by no group of this document.

THE ARTWORK — GROUPS 2, 3 AND 4

All rights reserved, with the narrow permissions below.

Groups 2 and 3: you may view, download and study these files. You may reference them in
commentary, review or discussion of this work, with attribution to Nthnkr "dpna" and AmandaBT and
a link to this repository.

Group 4: you may view these images and reference them in commentary, review or discussion of this
work, on the same attribution terms. Nothing further.

PROVENANCE

Files in groups 2 and 3 carry their origin inside them, in more than one form. Removing the
visible parts does not make a file anonymous, and does not affect the terms below.

WHAT YOU MAY NOT DO WITH THE ARTWORK

These files are published so that the work can be evaluated. They are not published for reuse.
Without prior written permission you may not:

  - redistribute them, altered or unaltered, as your own work or as part of any collection;
  - use them in any commercial context, including print, merchandise, tattooing, engraving or
    client work;
  - use them as training data for machine learning models of any kind;
  - register them, or any derivative of them, as a trademark or claim authorship of them.

The prohibitions on redistribution, model training and authorship claims are absolute and are not
lifted by any permission granted for other use.

These prohibitions bind the artwork only. They do not cut down the AGPL rights you have in the
code of group 1. A fork of the code that ships without the artwork is entirely permitted; a fork
that ships the artwork is not.

NO WARRANTY, AND NOT TAX ADVICE

Provided as is, without warranty of any kind. This is a research prototype in active development;
the samples reflect a state of the work at a moment in time and are not guaranteed to be stable,
correct or fit for any purpose.

The code in group 1 calculates Brazilian crypto taxation from rules documented in FONTES.md, each
carrying its source and the date it was last checked. Tax law changes, and the authors are not
your accountant. Nothing this software produces is tax advice, and responsibility for the figures
anyone files rests with the person who files them.

